{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"That’s too broad. Some white people benefit from lasting effects of historical racism, such as inherited wealth or unequal access to opportunities, even without participating in wrongdoing. But the extent varies across people and societies, and benefiting from an injustice is different from being personally responsible for it.\n\nA more defensible claim is that racial injustice can create systemic advantages for white people; it doesn’t establish that every white person benefits from every wrong committed by other white people."}}
